<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>This download is NOT verified yet: TeamViewer publishes no hash for the file, and a check of the signature is not built, so nothing proves that the file is what TeamViewer published. The shared importer therefore refuses a real run of the cimian recipe unless the override sets cimian_allow_unverified to true (pcman_allow_unverified for the package tool's recipe). Downloads the zip of TeamViewer's 64-bit MSI installers from https://download.teamviewer.com/download/version_15x/TeamViewer_MSI64.zip, which redirects to dl.teamviewer.com and needs no login. No page of TeamViewer names this address: it is known from third-party packaging scripts, not documented by the vendor, and may change or stop without notice. The zip holds a Full and a Host folder; the core processor Unarchiver unpacks it with Python's own zip code (USE_PYTHON_NATIVE_EXTRACTOR; in AutoPkg 2.9.0 and later it refuses a member that would land outside the folder, and older versions drop such parts of a name silently) into a folder of the recipe's cache that it empties first (purge_destination), so a file of an earlier run is never imported. The core processor FileFinder then names the one member TEAMVIEWER_MSI_MEMBER (default Host/TeamViewer_Host.msi) in that folder as found_filename, the file that the child recipes import; a zip without that member stops the run there, and nothing else in the zip is taken instead. The recipe never stops on an unchanged download, so a failed import is tried again at the next run.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.TeamViewerHost-Win</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>TeamViewerHost</string>
            <key>DOWNLOAD_URL</key>
            <string>https://download.teamviewer.com/download/version_15x/TeamViewer_MSI64.zip</string>
            <key>DOWNLOAD_FILENAME</key>
            <string>TeamViewer_MSI64.zip</string>
            <key>TEAMVIEWER_MSI_MEMBER</key>
            <string>Host/TeamViewer_Host.msi</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>URLDownloader</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>url</key>
                    <string>%DOWNLOAD_URL%</string>
                    <key>filename</key>
                    <string>%DOWNLOAD_FILENAME%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>EndOfCheckPhase</string>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>Unarchiver</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>archive_path</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                    <key>destination_path</key>
                    <string>%RECIPE_CACHE_DIR%/unpacked</string>
                    <key>purge_destination</key>
                    <true/>
                    <key>archive_format</key>
                    <string>zip</string>
                    <key>USE_PYTHON_NATIVE_EXTRACTOR</key>
                    <true/>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>FileFinder</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pattern</key>
                    <string>%RECIPE_CACHE_DIR%/unpacked/%TEAMVIEWER_MSI_MEMBER%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
